Day 68 and 69 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge
Today, I solved LeetCode 236 – Lowest Common Ancestor of a Binary Tree 
- Approach:
I used recursion to search for both nodes in the left and right subtrees.
If the current node is null, p, or q, return it.
Recursively search the left and right subtrees.
If both sides return a node, the current node is the LCA.
Otherwise, return whichever side contains a node.

Time: O(n)
Space: O(h) 

- Key Takeaways:
LCA can be solved elegantly using postorder-style recursion.
The return value from each subtree carries important information upward.
If both left and right contain one target, the current node is their lowest common ancestor.

